ion is directly correlated with brain transduction.\" ✓. SPR affinity ✓ (KD ∼20 nM). Cryo-EM 3-fold apex ✓ (\"protruding density on the apex of VR-IV at the 3-fold axis\"). \"predicted capsid–ALPL contact residues\" — from the May 2026 presentation (p1:c4 source), not the Cell paper; but the claim as a whole (\"has run the closest analogue... and predicted capsid–ALPL contact residues\") spans both sources; cited source here is the Cell paper. The negative claim (\"has not published exhaustive pose-depth sampling across a capsid panel with transcytose-versus-retain labels\") — consistent with the paper's contents (only DiffDock for inhibitors, no pose-depth sweeps). SUPPORTED with note that the contact-residues element is documented in the companion presentation.\n\n**p2:step** — quote verified on GitHub README ✓. Claims about scoring (atom-counting energy + binding-angle/pocket-depth geometry) verified in PMC11184338 (\"non-negative energetic binding score based on atom counting\", \"geometrical constraints... binding angle and pocket depth\"); classification receptor-dependent vs independent (\"APPRAISE can accurately classify receptor-dependent vs. receptor-independent adeno-associated viral vectors\") ✓; Colab ✓ (\"accessible through a web-based notebook interface using Google Colaboratory\"). Ten models per competition — verified in the companion paper. \"single-GPU Colab sessions\" — the paper says three parallel Colab GPU sessions for HT screen; per-model 0.1–1 GPU minutes. The step item says \"Today this runs at ten models per competition on single-GPU Colab sessions\" — fine. SUPPORTED.\n\n**p2:c3** — SUPPORTED (verbatim quote verified + ranking recovers binders + 10 replicate conditions).\n\n**p2:c4** — quote verified verbatim on PMC11381518 (PMC mirror of the Nature Comms article; the DOI source itself). \"single A100\" — verified via biorxiv PDF methods excerpt (\"We ran the Google Colaboratory notebook using an A100 SXM4 40GB GPU. Five structure models were produced...\") — that's the bioRxiv preprint, not the Nature Comms page. Hmm — the Nature Comms final version likely retains this methods text. The published version's methods (from my earlier truncated fetch of nature.com) — I didn't see the methods. But the PMC version (PMC11381518) is the published version and contains \"Five structure models were produced using a protocol with up to 20 recycles, and MSA generated with MMseqs2 (UniRef+Environmental) and templates from PDB70.\" ✓ (from search excerpt of PMC11381518). Does the published version mention A100? Probably in methods. I haven't seen it. The \"validated poses experimentally and on macaque/human primary brain microvascular endothelial cells\" claim — unverified so far. Let me do one more search round for these two details on the published paper.\n\n**p2:done** — quote \"Each model was recycled three times, and 10 models were generated from each competition.\" — not found via exact-phrase search. Need to check the Sci Adv methods. Let me search variants: \"recycled three times\" sciadv.adg6618, or \"3 recycles\" \"10 models\" Gradinaru APPRAISE-AAV. Let me also consider that the Sci Adv methods might state: \"Each model was recycled three times, and 10 models were generated from each competition\" — maybe it IS there but not indexed. Let me try fetching the PMC10115422 page in a different format (markdown) — truncation point may differ, possibly reaching Methods. The page total is ~130KB+; the fetch cut around 65KB of text. Format markdown might produce similar. Alternatively fetch with a \"#\" anchor won't help.\n\nAnother approach: Google Scholar / Europe PMC. Europe PMC has full text: https://europepmc.org/article/MED/37075114 — could fetch and it might show full text. Or use websearch with different phrasing: \"\\\"recycled three times\\\" APPRAISE LY6A\" (exact phrase \"recycled three times\").\n\nLet me do a batch:\n1. websearch: \"recycled three times\" APPRAISE AAV LY6A Ding Shay (exact phrase)\n2. websearch: s41467-024-52149-0 \"A100\" OR \"brain microvascular endothelial\" LRP6 validation — to check A100 in published version and BMVEC validation.\n3. Maybe fetch europepmc for the Sci Adv paper.\n\nLet me batch: two searches + one europepmc fetch."
